<div xmlns:perseus="http://www.perseus.org/meta/perseus.rdfs#" xmlns:dctype="http://purl.org/dc/dcmitype/" xmlns:tufts="http://www.tufts.edu/" xmlns:alph="http://alpheios.net/namespaces/tei" class="alpheios-lex-text_container en">
    <div class="alpheios-lex-entry" lemma-id="n100047" body-key=""><b><span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">συνεμ-βολή</span></b> , ἡ, <div class="alpheios-lex-lex_sense alpheios-lex-lex_sense1"><b>A.</b><i>throwing in together</i>,
				<span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">κώπης ῥοθιάδος ξ</span>. <i>the
				regular dip of all</i> the oars <i>together</i>, to the sound
			of the <span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">κέλευσμα</span>, <i><span class="en">
				A.
				<u>Pers.</u>
				396
			</span></i>:—in <i><span class="en">
				Id.
				<u>Ag.</u>
				984
			</span></i> (lyr.), <span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">πρυμνησίων
			ξυνεμβολάς</span> (<span class="entity">Headlam</span>) may be read
			for <span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">ξυνεμβόλοις</span>, in concrete sense
			the cables <i>cast out</i> from the stern.</div>
    </div> <div class="alpheios-lex-footnotes en"> </div>
